# MoonBit build output
/_build/

# Generated public interfaces. `moon info` writes these into every package
# root, and they carry their own warning: "DON'T EDIT IT". They are output,
# not source, so a change to any public signature would otherwise show up as
# an unrelated diff in every commit that happened to run a build.
*.generated.mbti

# Vendored dependencies. `moon add` re-fetches these from mooncakes.io; they
# are a cache, not source, and the lockfile in .mooncakes/ pins the versions.
/.mooncakes/

# The staged browser bundle is generated by build.ps1 from the js build.
# The shell (index.html, styles.css) is source and IS tracked.
/frontend/dist/main.js

# Local SQLite database
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Local server log captures from ad-hoc QA runs
/_s.log
/_s.err
/_s.out
/_stdout.txt
/_stderr.txt

# Ad-hoc diagnostic dumps written by a local server run. These are scratch
# evidence, never source: a run that writes them must not be able to commit
# them by accident.
/_dbg/
/_reqlog/

# Fixtures the backend tests write into the working directory. They are
# removed when the test finishes, but a test that dies leaves them behind,
# and a fixture in the tree is a file that looks like source.
/test_bootstrap_*
/test_agent_*

# Analysis output. LunaFlow and moonbit_static_analysis both write reports/
# into the working directory they are run in, and running one against this
# tree is a diagnostic, not a change to it: a report, its traces and its
# findings describe what an analyser thought of one run. Committing them would
# put a snapshot of that opinion in the history as though it were source, and
# the next run would overwrite it with a different snapshot.
/reports/
